In article <1990Oct3.003702.4181@midway.uchicago.edu> goer@quads.uchicago.edu (Richard L. Goerwitz) writes:
>I've always wanted to  be able to urge my pet on somewhere.  With
>real pets you can naturally shove them gently with your hand, or,
>if need be, your foot.  It would be silly, though, to expect the
>dev team to develop an "urge on" command.   Verbal commands are a
>bit much, too.

Perhaps it's extreme to add a whole new command, but there are other
similar ways around this.  Right now when you move into your pet it
says "You stop to avoid hitting <pet-name>" (unless you're confused
or hallucinating, etc.).  Instead of that, how about if it said
"Swap places with <pet-name> [yn]" ?  This certainly _seems_ like
a fairly small change to the game.

Also, the dead-end corridor is not the worst scenario.  My jackals
problem was far worse; my character was only about level 3 and he died
of starvation before he could slog his way through all his pets!  And
that was just because the stupid things didn't feel like moving!  I
guess one could say, "The moral is, don't keep lots of pets".  Somehow
that seems like a cop-out to me, though.

